# PEAK3 Arena — Web environment variables
# Copy to .env.local and fill in values (never commit .env.local)

# API base URL (where the FastAPI app is running)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# The canonical public origin of THIS deployment, e.g.
# https://peak3-staging.vercel.app — no trailing slash.
#
# Read by app/auth/callback/route.ts. Behind a proxy (Vercel), the request's
# own origin is the internal one, so the OAuth callback must redirect against
# the public origin taken from `x-forwarded-host`. That header is checked
# against an allowlist built from this value, so leaving it unset does not
# break the callback — it narrows the allowlist to the request's own host,
# which is correct but means a proxied host is refused rather than trusted.
# Set it in every deployed environment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app

# ---- Supabase Auth (optional — auth features disabled when unset) ----
#
# Both values below are PUBLIC by design: they are compiled into the browser
# bundle. Never put a service-role or secret key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable.
# `apps/api/tests/test_service_role_not_bundled.py` scans the built .next/
# output for one — but it SKIPS when .next/ has not been built, so run
# `npm run build` before relying on it.
#
# Your Supabase project URL: Settings > API > Project URL
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# Supabase anon (or publishable) key: Settings > API
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# ---- Sign-in providers ----
# Google OAuth and email magic link are implemented in the app but must also be
# enabled on the Supabase project, and every origin that completes a sign-in has
# to be listed under Authentication > URL Configuration > Redirect URLs:
#
#   http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#   https://your-production-domain/auth/callback
#
# The app additionally validates every `next`/`returnTo` with safeNext() before
# redirecting, so provider allowlisting and application validation are both in
# force. Full setup steps: docs/implementation/AUTH_CONFIGURATION.md
#
# Sessions are cookie-based (@supabase/ssr) and refreshed by
# apps/web/src/middleware.ts — note that middleware lives under src/, because
# Next resolves it relative to the directory containing app/.

# ---- Product telemetry (Track F) — OFF unless explicitly turned on ----
#
# Set to exactly "true" to make the browser client send collected product
# events to POST /api/v1/telemetry/events (see src/lib/analytics.ts). Anything
# else — including unset — and the client never makes the request at all.
#
# BOTH SIDES MUST AGREE. The API has its own independent switch,
# PEAK3_TELEMETRY_ENABLED (apps/api/.env.example), and is likewise off by
# default. Turning on only this one produces requests the API refuses with 403;
# turning on only the API's produces an endpoint nothing calls. That is
# deliberate for a privacy-affecting collection path: it cannot be enabled by
# accident on one side.
#
# The dev-console sink (`console.debug`) is unaffected by this and never sends
# anything anywhere.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=true

# ---- E2E auth mode (tests only — NEVER set this on a deployment) ----
#
# Renders the account surface (the /signin and /signup pages, the header
# account control, the mobile account section) with NO hosted Supabase project
# behind it. Nothing else changes: no Supabase client is constructed, so no
# request reaches Google, a project, or a mailbox, and every real sign-in flow
# still returns "Auth not configured".
#
# It exists because those surfaces used to be gated on credentials being
# present, so a developer with a .env.local ran a different application from
# CI — and ten browser assertions about copy, returnTo propagation, initials
# avatars and sign-out passed locally and failed on a clean checkout.
#
# `npm run dev:e2e` sets it, and playwright.config.ts starts the web server
# with that script. It CANNOT take effect in a production build:
# `process.env.NODE_ENV !== "production"` is inlined at build time and folds
# the whole branch away (see src/lib/supabase/config.ts).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PEAK3_E2E_AUTH=1
